# Code ownership map.
# Mirrors docs/43-development-standards.md Sec.8.1. Keep in sync with that
# doc; amendments here require a `policy`-scoped PR.
#
# Review semantics:
#   - Primary reviewer is the default approver.
#   - For PRs authored by the primary reviewer, the deputy reviewer
#     performs the review (conflict-of-interest rule, Sec.8.3). If both
#     are unavailable, the PR waits with the `succession-pending` label.
#   - Architecture-impacting PRs require AO + Independent Architecture
#     Reviewer sign-off per Sec.8.2.
#   - Subtrees marked NON-DELEGABLE have only the AO as approver; the
#     Deputy cannot self-merge even under T1 succession.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TODO(deputy-handle): The Deputy reviewer GitHub handle is intentionally
# omitted from every entry below until a real account is confirmed. The
# policy docs (docs/43-development-standards.md Sec.8.1 and
# docs/23-decision-ownership-matrix.md) still describe the Deputy role;
# this file holds only the AO handle until the Deputy joins.
#
# When the Deputy handle is known, a follow-up `policy`-scoped PR will:
#   1. Add the Deputy to every non-NON-DELEGABLE line below (catch-all,
#      engine/, integrations/, app/, release-eng/, .github/workflows/,
#      docs/).
#   2. Bump `required_approving_review_count` from 0 to 1 in branch
#      protection so the Sec.8.3 conflict-of-interest rule becomes
#      mechanically enforceable.
#
# Do NOT add a placeholder handle here — CODEOWNERS with a non-existent
# GitHub account silently disables code-owner review for matched paths.
# Tracked by PhantasticUniverse/chromaticity Issue #3.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

